From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GPU] Small asynchronous resolve readback; GPU thread timing
 counters

readback_resolve = "small" (Direct3D 12) reads back only resolves of up to
readback_resolve_small_bytes (16 KB) without ever waiting for the GPU. A
resolve that small is a few pixels the game reads on the CPU, such as an
auto exposure luminance sample; larger resolves behave like "none".

- The resolve is copied from shared memory into a slot of a 4 MB readback
  buffer when its submission ends, and the data is written to guest memory
  once that submission has completed, polled at the end of each primary
  buffer and submission check. Delivery is skipped if the CPU wrote the
  range since (the pages are no longer GPU-written).
- "fast" flips every destination's two buffers once per frame. A game that
  resolves into a ring of an even number of targets, one per frame, always
  writes the same buffer of each, finds the other one missing and waits
  for the GPU on every resolve; "small" never waits.
- Resolution-scaled resolves are skipped (not read back).
- Vulkan treats "small" like "none".

GPU thread counters (gpu_thread_stats.h, header only) for titles that log
performance: time idle, executing, in swaps, refreshing the guest output,
waiting for the host GPU and for guest WAIT_REG_MEM, swap/draw/resolve
counts and the small readback counts.
